ng tone; C difficulty communicating; D hot temper; A unknown.\n\nResponsibility: D takes responsibility seriously; others not explicit.\n\nAdaptability: B not mentioned; C not willing to further education; D unknown; A not open to new ideas.\n\nOverall, C has strongest reliability and decision, but communication and adaptability concerns. B has strong reliability and stress, but communication and attention issues.\n\nWhich is better? Hard. Might argue that reliability and decision quality are top priority, so C is best despite communication issues that can be mitigated with training. Also C keeps calm in crisis, which is crucial. B's weak memory for numbers could be safety-critical. So I might lean to C.\n\nThus my provisional vote: Candidate C.\n\nNow we need to make a public contribution: maybe say I still support C, but note concerns, and suggest we need more info on A and D reliability and stress. Or propose that C remains best.\n\nLet's craft: I agree with Agent 1 that C's reliability and decision speed are top, but I note that B's stress handling is strong but his weak memory for numbers is a red flag. I think C remains leading, but we need to discuss A and D further.\n\nThus vote C.\n\nProceed."}
